could be shipped): `. ./role.sh`, `. ./helper-base.sh`, `hork__is_converged`, `.
./helper-variant.sh`, `hork__is_converged`, `hork__is_converged` -- run `dorc
why` for the per-site detail (the apply runs each anyway, to stay safe)
      [ book.sh:15:1
   15 | . ./role.sh
      | \_________/

   = help:  sm site runs `. ./role.sh`
hint: '.' (line 15) is unmodeled: it is the first wall -- an oracle vouching its convergence would elide it when converged; 5 more unmodeled walls -- dorc why
